From: MediaBox
Subject: hwdec_drmprime: accept Rockchip's NV15 and NV20

Rockchip MPP decodes ten-bit HEVC into NV15, a packed format upstream
ffmpeg does not define and the appliance's ffmpeg fork does. mpv already
has a mechanism for exactly this -- it looks fork-specific pixel formats
up by name -- and the list simply did not have these two in it.
--- a/video/out/hwdec/hwdec_drmprime.c
+++ b/video/out/hwdec/hwdec_drmprime.c
@@ -75,6 +75,12 @@
 static const char *forked_pix_fmt_names[] = {
     "rpi4_8",
     "rpi4_10",
+    /* Rockchip MPP decodes ten-bit HEVC into NV15, a packed format that
+     * upstream ffmpeg does not define. The RK3588 display controller scans it
+     * out directly, so nothing has to convert it; mpv only has to stop
+     * refusing a frame whose name it does not recognise. */
+    "nv15",
+    "nv20",
 };
 
 static int init(struct ra_hwdec *hw)
